    {
      "el": "**The three words.** *Enforced*: this worker builds the property in its own code, and a test reads it back off what was produced. *Asserted*: something outside the worker provides it (an image, a vendor's documentation), which the worker cannot verify. *Absent*: not provided, so a floor that asks for it refuses this venue. *With the image* means only from a job image that declares the feature.",
      "kind": "readme",
      "status": "new",
      "source": "admin/src/console/panels/venue.mjs#venueProperties",
      "golden": [
        "panels/venue-openshell.operator"
      ],
      "shows": [
        "enforced",
        "asserted",
        "absent",
        "not verifiable from here",
        "not provided"
      ],
      "panel": "p-venue-props"
    },
    {
      "el": "**Where the words come from.** What a venue declares is this build's table. Which hosts bless it, their floors and their OpenShell setup are what each host's worker published when it started.",
      "kind": "readme",
      "status": "new",
      "source": "admin/src/console/panels/venue.mjs#venueSummary",
      "golden": [
        "panels/venue-openshell.operator"
